Cell[TextData[{
 "The quotient map of a model is a quasi-isomorphism exactly when the model \
is of Hodge type, which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["HodgeTypeQ"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/HodgeTypeQ", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0061abe8-a8f3-493c-970d-7fbd85be2069"],
 " decides. On a model that is not, the algebra is still built and is still a \
Poincar\[EAcute] duality algebra, but it no longer carries the model's \
homotopy type."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d7960a03-6657-4cae-9c66-c10443c270e0"],

Cell["\<\
The algebra displays as a summary box: its basis and its degree, with the \
degrees, the Gram matrix, the differential and the model under the opener.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b4fa7e6c-8668-4fd7-8a30-9bca79c74744"]
}, Open  ]],

